# Keep the deploy upload lean — none of this is needed at runtime, and the
# Docker build reinstalls deps + rebuilds the client from source. A bloated
# upload (the ~284MB marketing/ dir, node_modules, dist) was timing out
# `railway up` mid-transfer and dying at INITIALIZING.
# docs/emails is the ONE exception: scripts/send-announcement.js reads the
# template at runtime, and it can only run in the container because that's where
# the user list lives. Written as `docs/*` + a negation because gitignore syntax
# cannot re-include anything under an excluded directory.
docs/*
!docs/emails/
design-v2/
.agents/
marketing/
node_modules/
client/node_modules/
client/dist/
.git/
*.log
.DS_Store
